-- Fixture for the `l4 run` crashed-#EVAL exit-code rule (ruled by Meng
-- 2026-08-01): a directive that CRASHES during evaluation must exit non-zero.
--
-- This file must TYPECHECK (so the run is not failed by a type error instead —
-- which would make the test pass for the wrong reason) and must THROW when the
-- directive is evaluated. `@nonexhaustive` silences the exhaustiveness warning
-- the oracle would otherwise emit, leaving a CONSIDER with no NOTHING branch;
-- evaluating it against NOTHING reaches no branch and raises the runtime
-- non-exhaustive-match exception.
§ EvalCrashFixture

@nonexhaustive
GIVEN mx IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
unwrap mx MEANS
  CONSIDER mx
  WHEN JUST n THEN n

#EVAL unwrap NOTHING
